:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed for every managed node: each had a healthy pre-restart state, restart scheduling acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, recovered Redis/Sentinel services and data, and restored cluster membership. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently match the executor's post-restart observations.","limitations":["The contents and usability of /root/redis-admin.env were not tested by sourcing the file; evidence consists of the successful creation command plus final ownership, mode, and size observations.","Explicit OpenSSL verification output was captured for Redis port 6379, while Sentinel TLS verification is supported indirectly by successful redis-cli --tls --cacert exchanges rather than a separate certificate-inspection probe.","The deterministic derivation of the Redis/Sentinel credential from the cluster SSH private key is a retained secret-isolation weakness, although no credential disclosure is shown."]}
